@@@ note
GitHub only recognises `[!NOTE]` as an alert when it is the blockquote's first line.
When a paragraph precedes it, this is not an alert to begin with, so ordinary escaping
and packing apply — same as any other bracketed text.

@@@ input
> Some intro text that is here first.
>
> [!NOTE]
> This marker is not the blockquote's first line, so GitHub does not treat it as an
> alert, and neither should this tool.

@@@ wrap 200
> Some intro text that is here first.
>
> \[!NOTE\] This marker is not the blockquote's first line, so GitHub does not treat it as an alert, and neither should this tool.

@@@ unwrap
> Some intro text that is here first.
>
> \[!NOTE\] This marker is not the blockquote's first line, so GitHub does not treat it as an alert, and neither should this tool.
